  "clock_transition:not-on-D1 (clock_transition runs on M1/M5/M15/M30/H1 only -- the whole mechanism is ONE named stamp-hour -- a fix, a settlement, a handoff, a rollover -- and it already refuses a stamp hour the bars do not carry; declaring the domain says so before the sweep spends a pass discovering it on every symbol)": 6,
  "clock_transition:not-on-H4 (clock_transition runs on M1/M5/M15/M30/H1 only -- the whole mechanism is ONE named stamp-hour -- a fix, a settlement, a handoff, a rollover -- and it already refuses a stamp hour the bars do not carry; declaring the domain says so before the sweep spends a pass discovering it on every symbol)": 5,
  "correlation_regime:not-on-M15 (correlation_regime runs on H1/H4/D1 only -- same bar-for-bar join as relative_value: a correlation BREAKDOWN measured on M1 bars across instruments with different quoting hours is a measurement of the quoting hours)": 1,
  "cross_asset_residual:not-on-M15 (cross_asset_residual runs on H1/H4/D1 only -- projects out several factor instruments bar for bar; below the hour the factor betas are biased toward zero by non-synchronous quoting and the 'unexplained' residual is mostly the asynchrony. The same reason keeps the eight-frame factor basket off the fine charts)": 1,
  "execution_state:not-on-D1 (execution_state runs on M1/M5/M15/M30/H1 only -- the surface it reads is published by (weekday, STAMP HOUR), so a bar spanning four hours or a day cannot be placed in one of its buckets -- the family would return [] on every symbol there and be filed as a data gap rather than as an inexpressible claim)": 6,
  "execution_state:not-on-H4 (execution_state runs on M1/M5/M15/M30/H1 only -- the surface it reads is published by (weekday, STAMP HOUR), so a bar spanning four hours or a day cannot be placed in one of its buckets -- the family would return [] on every symbol there and be filed as a data gap rather than as an inexpressible claim)": 5,
  "fx_fixing_reversal:not-on-D1 (fx_fixing_reversal runs on M1/M5/M15/M30/H1 only -- the claim is about the hour containing the 16:00 London fix; a four-hour or daily bar cannot locate a fix, and the pre-fix window it measures is minutes to an hour wide)": 6,
  "fx_fixing_reversal:not-on-H4 (fx_fixing_reversal runs on M1/M5/M15/M30/H1 only -- the claim is about the hour containing the 16:00 London fix; a four-hour or daily bar cannot locate a fix, and the pre-fix window it measures is minutes to an hour wide)": 5,
  "generic:not-on-D1 (generic runs on M1/M5/M15/M30/H1 only -- its CONTEXT vocabulary is broker-hour session windows (asia/london/new_york/overlap); on a four-hour bar those masks resolve to two or three stamps a day and on a daily bar to none at all, so a coordinate naming a session would be tested somewhere else entirely. The OUTPUT horizons ('1h', '4h', 'daily') are converted to the chart's own bars by `family_generic._hold_bars`, so they mean the same market time on every chart here)": 6,
  "generic:not-on-H4 (generic runs on M1/M5/M15/M30/H1 only -- its CONTEXT vocabulary is broker-hour session windows (asia/london/new_york/overlap); on a four-hour bar those masks resolve to two or three stamps a day and on a daily bar to none at all, so a coordinate naming a session would be tested somewhere else entirely. The OUTPUT horizons ('1h', '4h', 'daily') are converted to the chart's own bars by `family_generic._hold_bars`, so they mean the same market time on every chart here)": 5,
  "hedging_demand_close:not-on-D1 (hedging_demand_close runs on M1/M5/M15/M30/H1 only -- fires in the institutional closing HOUR (close_hour, a broker stamp-hour); a chart whose bars span four hours or a day cannot carry that hour, so the family would return [] on every symbol and be filed as a data gap rather than as an inexpressible claim)": 6,
  "hedging_demand_close:not-on-H4 (hedging_demand_close runs on M1/M5/M15/M30/H1 only -- fires in the institutional closing HOUR (close_hour, a broker stamp-hour); a chart whose bars span four hours or a day cannot carry that hour, so the family would return [] on every symbol and be filed as a data gap rather than as an inexpressible claim)": 5,
  "lvc_asia_london:not-on-D1 (lvc_asia_london runs on M5 only -- a source-faithful reproduction of a public EA whose defaults are pinned to a named blob and whose windows are M5-bar counts (recent_extreme_bars=3 is fifteen minutes). Run on another chart it is no longer the thing it reproduces, and the ablation it exists to settle would be answered about a different strategy)": 6,
  "lvc_asia_london:not-on-H1 (lvc_asia_london runs on M5 only -- a source-faithful reproduction of a public EA whose defaults are pinned to a named blob and whose windows are M5-bar counts (recent_extreme_bars=3 is fifteen minutes). Run on another chart it is no longer the thing it reproduces, and the ablation it exists to settle would be answered about a different strategy)": 5,
  "lvc_asia_london:not-on-H4 (lvc_asia_london runs on M5 only -- a source-faithful reproduction of a public EA whose defaults are pinned to a named blob and whose windows are M5-bar counts (recent_extreme_bars=3 is fifteen minutes). Run on another chart it is no longer the thing it reproduces, and the ablation it exists to settle would be answered about a different strategy)": 5,
  "lvc_asia_london:not-on-M15 (lvc_asia_london runs on M5 only -- a source-faithful reproduction of a public EA whose defaults are pinned to a named blob and whose windows are M5-bar counts (recent_extreme_bars=3 is fifteen minutes). Run on another chart it is no longer the thing it reproduces, and the ablation it exists to settle would be answered about a different strategy)": 1,
  "macro_conditional:not-on-M15 (macro_conditional runs on H1/H4/D1 only -- the conditioning variable is a DAILY FRED print, lagged a publication day and forward-filled; emitting a decision on every M1 bar asserts 1,440 independent decisions a day from a number that moves once. Below the hour this multiplies cells without adding one bit of information, which is the definition of a meaningless cell)": 1,
  "opening_range:not-on-D1 (opening_range runs on M1/M5/M15/M30/H1 only -- the range forms in the first bars after ONE named stamp-hour (open_hour, the cash open); a four-hour bar stamped 0/4/8/12/16/20 carries stamp 10 on no day and a daily bar carries no hour at all, so the family would return [] on every symbol there and be filed as a data gap rather than as an inexpressible claim)": 6,
  "opening_range:not-on-H4 (opening_range runs on M1/M5/M15/M30/H1 only -- the range forms in the first bars after ONE named stamp-hour (open_hour, the cash open); a four-hour bar stamped 0/4/8/12/16/20 carries stamp 10 on no day and a daily bar carries no hour at all, so the family would return [] on every symbol there and be filed as a data gap rather than as an inexpressible claim)": 5,
  "pca_residual:not-on-M15 (pca_residual runs on H1/H4/D1 only -- extracts the universe's latent factors from a correlation matrix of factor instruments; at sub-hourly sampling that matrix is dominated by asynchronous quoting, and a Marchenko-Pastur cut on a noise structure that is not sampling noise keeps the wrong eigenvalues)": 1,
  "relative_value:not-on-M15 (relative_value runs on H1/H4/D1 only -- joins this instrument to a peer BAR FOR BAR. Below the hour that join measures non-synchronous trading rather than a common factor -- an equity CFD prints only in its cash session while an FX cross prints around the clock -- so the inner join collapses and the residual is an artifact of quoting hours (the Scholes-Williams problem))": 1,
  "session_handoff:not-on-D1 (session_handoff runs on M1/M5/M15/M30/H1 only -- reads one session's first bars and trades a later session's named hour; both ends of the claim are stamp-hours, which a bar spanning four hours or a day does not resolve)": 6,
  "session_handoff:not-on-H4 (session_handoff runs on M1/M5/M15/M30/H1 only -- reads one session's first bars and trades a later session's named hour; both ends of the claim are stamp-hours, which a bar spanning four hours or a day does not resolve)": 5
